                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "9v":</h3><p><img class="thumb shaft" src="http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Panasonic-PP3-9volt-battery.jpg/80px-Panasonic-PP3-9volt-battery.jpg" /><b>9V</b> indicates a type of battery, commonly called a &#8220;nine volt&#8221; but also (more officially) a <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PP3_battery">PP3 battery</a>. Microphones tagged &#8216;9V&#8217; can be operated <em>without</em> phantom power, via an onboard 9V battery. Note that such microphones are usually electret condensers; dynamic mics (including passive ribbons) do not need power, and externally-biased condensers need more that 9V.</p>
